## Claude Code agent instructions

<!-- V2: deep per-agent optimisation is deferred to HU-047 §10 Fase 2; this is the valid V1 minimum. -->

Claude Code reads `CLAUDE.md`, not `AGENTS.md`. Keep one source of truth:

- If `CLAUDE.md` exists, make it a pointer: its first line tells the agent to read `AGENTS.md`, and
  nothing from that file is duplicated here.
- Keep the FlowForge phase rules, checkpoint table and skill index in `AGENTS.md` only.
- Project slash commands are declared under `.claude/commands/`; the FlowForge `/flow-*` commands
  stay documented in the `AGENTS.md` index.
- Load a skill by reading its `SKILL.md` path from the index on demand, and respect CKP-0 through
  CKP-3 exactly as `AGENTS.md` describes.
